Optional OpenAI4S hook for the OpenMHS developer overlay (integration/openai4s).

Not required: the MCP connector rows and the governed host route need only
openai4s-core.patch. This hook appends one guarded block to openai4s/__init__.py so
that `import openai4s` calls openai4s_mhs.install(), which registers the native
mhs_* developer tools only while the MHS integration is enabled.

Upstream: https://github.com/PKU-YuanGroup/OpenAI4S.git
Base-Commit: f48f216c81fe400444857c8a5d84d7407398918c
OpenAI4S-Version: 0.3.1
Files: openai4s/__init__.py
Check: python3 -m openai4s_mhs core-patch check --overlay
Apply: git -C <OpenAI4S checkout at Base-Commit> apply <this file>

diff --git a/openai4s/__init__.py b/openai4s/__init__.py
index e98d45855bea526ad97a45a6a7c5f6f48cb0dad8..4c5b3edf1507e8122ea5f797e8a97e76b9077e3d 100644
--- a/openai4s/__init__.py
+++ b/openai4s/__init__.py
@@ -5,3 +5,13 @@ persistent kernel. Linux daemon form-factor.
 """
 
 __version__ = "0.3.1"
+
+# Optional OpenMHS developer overlay (integration/openai4s).  Importing it
+# registers the mhs_* tools and HostDispatcher methods while the MHS integration
+# is enabled; a missing overlay or SDK must never make `import openai4s` fail.
+try:
+    import openai4s_mhs
+
+    openai4s_mhs.install()
+except Exception:
+    pass
